2026-09-03T09:38Z claude note unaffected by the ladder re-cut, and deliberately so. The pack format has no outline field -- it is metadata + page catalog + typed blocks -- and a PDF's embedded table of contents is document metadata, not page content, so carrying it in a pack would need a field of ours that 0606's condition 2 forbids. This stays a segmenter tier and its TOC stays its own signal provenance, which is how the ratified interface already enumerates it. Correction to that same line, below.

2026-09-03T09:48Z claude note THIS TICKET IS SUBSTANTIALLY ALREADY BUILT, and was filed without reading the fork's state. `extractPdfOutline` in `fork/src/features/fulltext/pdf-pages.ts`, written 2026-08-31 -- a day before tracker 0557 was filed -- covers actions 1 to 5: `pdfjs-dist` ^5.6.205 declared and installed (action 1), `doc.getOutline()` (action 2), `dest` resolved through `getDestination`/`getPageIndex` to a 1-based page (action 3), an ordered walk emitting `{title, page, level}` with nesting preserved as `level` rather than flattened (action 4), and the empty case handled BETTER than this ticket asked -- it returns `[]` for a PDF with no outline and `null` for one that could not be read at all, a distinction the ticket's action 5 conflates. A dangling destination costs that heading its page, not the whole outline. Upstream shipped the surrounding work too: issue #29 closed COMPLETED 2026-08-29 as `f1d93cf` with a PDF outline and real page ranges (SYNC.md). WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED, and is what remains of this ticket: the version is a caret range, not the pinned version the first exit criterion requires; and no fixture test over an outlined PDF, a nested outline and a no-outline PDF has been confirmed to exist. So this needs a closeout audit against its exit criteria, not an implementation.

--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracker 0557. `pdf.js` (`mozilla/pdf.js`, Apache-2.0, confirmed
from its LICENSE file) is the ruled segmenter substrate -- JS-native,
license-clean against zoteus's MIT license, unlike the AGPL `PyMuPDF`/
`fitz` the same survey found and rejected. `getOutline()` returns the
PDF's embedded bookmark tree (the `/Outlines` catalog): title, and a
`dest` per node that must be resolved to a page index, not a page number
directly.

## Actions

1. Vendor `pdf.js` (or `pdfjs-dist` for Node) at a pinned version.
2. Given a PDF path/stream (from 0558), call `getOutline()`.
3. Resolve each node's `dest` to a page index via
   `pdfDocument.getPageIndex(destRef)`.
4. Build the ordered `{title, start_page}` list from the (possibly nested)
   outline tree; nesting itself is a signal (front/back matter and
   sub-sections) worth preserving, not flattening away.
5. `getOutline()` returns `null` when no outline exists -- this is the
   clean, already-anticipated trigger into tier 2 (ticket 0561), not an
   error.

## Test

- Fixture PDFs with a real embedded outline (many LaTeX/Word-exported PDFs
  carry one) and one confirmed to have none -- assert the second produces
  a clean `null`/empty result, not a crash or a wrong guess.
- A nested outline (parts containing chapters) -- assert nesting survives.

## Invariants

- Author is NOT expected from this tier -- no embedded outline carries
  contributor bylines. That's ticket 0562, applied on top of whatever
  boundaries tier 1 or tier 2 finds.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `pdf.js` vendored at a pinned version
- [ ] outline extraction + dest-to-page resolution implemented and tested
- [ ] clean `null` handling verified against a no-outline fixture
